      "added_fields": [
        {
          "note_id": "ByG1QoMxz",
          "fields": {
            "display_title": "Modern-day neural networks require code generation (to generate the backward pass) and a host of other optimizations to be run effectively. The paper proposes to do this using best practices in the compilers and programming languages communities as opposed to the ad hoc manner adopted by current deep learning engines. ",
            "replying_to": "Replying to DLVM: A modern compiler infrastructure for deep learning systems"
          }
        },
        {
          "note_id": "rJs8O8Bgz",
          "fields": {
            "display_title": "The paper presents a compiler framework for domain-specific languages (DSLs) targeting deep learning systems. The paper describes the overall structure, the different compilation stages, and also provides a small example. This type of frameworks is very useful and can have a significant impact in the community. However, no evaluation of the proposed framework is done in the paper.",
            "replying_to": "Replying to DLVM: A modern compiler infrastructure for deep learning systems"
          }
        },
        {
          "note_id": "SJ_WummXM",
          "fields": {
            "display_title": "A tensor compiler (as opposed to a DSL inside a general purpose language)",
            "replying_to": "Replying to DLVM: A modern compiler infrastructure for deep learning systems"
          }
